{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e881c9e3a4511aaa","name":"Subelectronic Converter","source":{"id":"source:reference-e881c9e3a4511aaa","title":"Subelectronic Converter","revision":26013,"timestamp":"2025-01-15T18:25:49Z","sha256":"397ca9dc11e1a8c72c853cf2261039efa8856e777ee718eeaf2d3eb25072c0cf","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26013","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Subelectronic%20Converter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e881c9e3a4511aaa","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 23,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed by Imperial scientist ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nasdra Magrody"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nasdra_Magrody?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the Subelectronic Converter is a computerized device that, when implanted into a subject's head, allows the subject to control ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," through ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". One such recipient of the cybernetic device, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Irek Ismaren"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Irek_Ismaren","referenceId":"reference:645d9e27f712fe5f"},", could mentally visualize a Droid's programming and use his ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mind Trick"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mind_Trick","referenceId":"reference:5c0f83fb6ec25f33"}]}," Force Power on them, which normally cannot be done. A Subelectronic Converter translates the signals from the subject's brain into ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"}," commands understood by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},"; likewise, it converts ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," signals into a language that the brain can understand.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Subelectronic Converter is just like any other cybernetic enhancement, in that it must be installed by a character with the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybernetic Surgery"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybernetic_Surgery","referenceId":"reference:27fcc9e886ed5a6d"}," feat and imposes a penalty on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," checks. A character with a Subelectronic Converter may use [",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mind-Affecting"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mind-Affecting"}]},"] Force Powers on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"},", despite the Droids' immunity to Mind-Affecting effects. However, there's a trade off: the recipient of the Subelectronic Converter takes a -2 penalty to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"}," due to side effects of the device.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
